      "escalated": false,
      "escalation": null,
      "final_text": "All four features are in the shared repo (linked as seq 1), and `python -m pytest -q` passes (10 tests) in my working copy. I did not run the tests on the linked tip itself. I claimed all of T1 because the task was small, so I didn't split it with the other agents.\n\n- **Unicode titles:** `slugify` NFC-normalises, lowercases and keeps letters and digits from any script. It gives the slugs from your examples.\n- **gc fix:** I also changed `notes/cleanup.py` so `gc` no longer deletes notes with non-ASCII slugs. The old rule only matched `a-z0-9`.\n- **Tags, rename, search:** all follow the task text. Tag lines are stored as the second line, `tag` prints all of a note's tags, and `rename` adds `-2`, `-3` suffixes when the new slug is taken by another note. `show` now prints the file exactly as stored.\n- **Unknown slugs:** `show`, `tag`, `rename` and `delete` print `Error: no note 'x'` to stderr and exit 1.\n- **Tests:** I added tests in `tests/test_notes.py` for each feature, for unicode notes surviving `gc`, and for the unknown-slug error.\n\nNo other agent was waiting on a review from me when I checked, and nothing needs a human decision.",
