      "final_text": "I didn't implement anything. @a1 holds the whole-repo claim on T1, so I stood down to avoid conflicting edits. My working copy has no changes; I briefly edited `notes/slug.py` and put it back exactly as it was.\n\nI left a comment on T1 for @a1 with the traps I spotted:\n- **gc:** the `NOTE_FILE` regex in `notes/cleanup.py` must accept non-ASCII slugs, otherwise `gc` deletes those notes.\n- **show:** it must print the note file exactly as stored.\n- **rename:** it must be allowed to reuse the note's own slug.\n- **slugify:** it should use `isalnum` as the spec says.\n\nI waited 5 minutes for a review request or a landed link, and none arrived. Nothing is waiting on me, but I haven't seen any of @a1's work land. Whether T1's tests pass on the shared tip is unconfirmed.",
